## Summary & Impact

`ttnn::moe_routing_remap` (`ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/data_movement/moe_routing_remap/`), `ttnn::moe_expert_token_remap` (`ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/data_movement/moe_expert_token_remap/`), `ttnn::experimental::topk_router_gpt` (`ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/experimental/topk_router_gpt/`), `ttnn::transformer::gated_delta_attn` (`ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/transformer/gated_delta_attn/`), and `ttnn::transformer::fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule` (`ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/transformer/fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule/`) form the core Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) routing/remapping and Gated Delta Rule linear attention paths in TTNN, and several were recently migrated to the Metal 2.0 `ProgramDescriptor` / `DataflowBuffer` API.

However, **8 coupled defects** across their host program factories, validators, RISC-V dataflow kernels, and Tensix compute kernels cause **silent misclassification of IEEE-754 `-0.0` expert weights**, **up to 256 KB out-of-bounds L1 memory corruption**, **100% deterministic `~DataflowBuffer() -> finish_impl()` drain deadlocks on Quasar**, **unaligned 8-byte NOC `async_write` source addresses**, **wrong unpacker `reduce_uninit` CB restoration and missing `pack_init` retargeting**, and **permanent device hangs**:

| # | Component | Defect | Impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | `moe_routing_remap` (`reader_moe_routing_remap.cpp:23, 46, 50-62`) | Casts `BFLOAT16`/`FLOAT32` routing weights to unsigned integer (`uint16_t`/`uint32_t`) and checks `if (val != 0)`. In IEEE-754, negative zero (`-0.0bf16 = 0x8000`, `-0.0f = 0x80000000`) has a non-zero bit pattern (`0x8000 != 0`) | **Silent MoE routing corruption**: `-0.0` inactive expert weights are misclassified as active non-zero experts, stealing `num_non_zero_per_device` slots, shifting `weight_offset_count` across cluster devices, and dropping real active experts |
| **2** | `moe_routing_remap` (`reader_moe_routing_remap.cpp:49-64`, `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp:36-64`) | (a) When a row has fewer than `non_zero_weight_size` non-zero weights (e.g., dropped tokens / zeroed gates), `local_weight_idx_ptr[device_weights_count .. num_non_zero_per_device - 1]` remains uninitialized in L1 (`c_1`), and `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp:49-53` unconditionally loops `num_non_zero_per_device` times calling `tt_memmove` with uninitialized `uint16_t` indices; (b) `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp` exits without calling `pop_front(1)` on `routing_weights_dfb`, `local_weights_idxs_dfb`, or `local_weights_dfb` | **Up to `65535 * datum_size` (128 KB–256 KB) out-of-bounds L1 memory corruption** and **100% deterministic `~DataflowBuffer() -> finish_impl()` drain deadlock on Quasar** |
| **3** | `moe_expert_token_remap` (`moe_expert_token_remap_program_factory.cpp:49-50, 121-145`, `writer_moe_expert_token_remap.cpp:46, 110`, `moe_expert_token_remap_device_operation.cpp:15-105`) | (a) Unlike `c_0..c_3`, CBs `c_4` (`output_mapping_cb_id`) and `c_5` (`output_reduced_cb_id`) set `.total_size` and `.page_size` to raw unaligned `experts_per_device * 2` bytes; when `experts_per_device % 8 != 0` (e.g. 16 experts across 4 devices -> `4 * 2 = 8` bytes), `c_5` is placed at an 8-byte-aligned L1 address and `writer_moe_expert_token_remap.cpp` issues `noc.async_write` from non-16B-aligned L1 addresses; (b) `validate_on_program_cache_miss` never checks `experts % num_devices == 0`, `metadata_shape[2] == topk_shape[2]`, or preallocated output shapes/layouts | **Unaligned 8-byte NOC `async_write` L1 source address violation** and **silent integer truncation / OOB reads on mismatched shapes** |
| **4** | `topk_router_gpt` (`topk_router_gpt_program_factory.cpp:91-106, 535, 563`) | `create_descriptor` allocates CBs/semaphores and launches `{DM0, DM1, COMPUTE}` on `all_cores` (`num_cores` DRAM bank worker cores) at line 535, but only populates runtime args for `required_cores` (`8` or `12`) cores at line 563 | **100% deterministic device hang** whenever `num_cores > required_cores` (extra cores run with zeroed runtime args `is_sender = 0`, enter the worker path, and block forever on `dfb_partial_recv.wait_front(num_senders)` and `partial_sem.wait(num_senders)`), or host `std::vector` OOB read if `num_cores < required_cores` |
| **5** | `topk_router_gpt` (`compute.cpp:118-314`, `dm1.cpp:113-324`, `topk_router_gpt_device_operation.cpp:26`) | (a) `compute.cpp:252, 287` calls `reduce_uninit(dfb::reduce_scalar)` passing the **output** DFB (`ocb`) instead of the **input** DFB (`icb = dfb::softmax_tmp`) required by `reduce_uninit(std::uint32_t icb)`; (b) `compute.cpp` switches pack targets across 7 DFBs (`local_out`, `topk_val`, `intermed_val`, `intermed_ind`, `softmax_tmp`, `reduce_scalar`, `final_out`) without `#ifdef ARCH_QUASAR pack_init(...); #endif`; (c) `dm1.cpp:207, 236, 247, 268` reads and pops `dfb_index` without calling `dfb_index.wait_front(1)`, and calls `get_write_ptr()` on `dfb_partial_recv`, `dfb_gathered_val`, and `dfb_gathered_ind` before `reserve_back`; (d) `hidden_dim == 0` passes `hidden_dim % 32 == 0` validation | **Wrong unpacker state after `reduce_uninit`, pack target misrouting on Quasar (`#58488`), unbalanced DFB lifecycle on `dfb_index`, and invalid zero-dimension launch** |
| **6** | `gated_delta_attn` (`gated_delta_attn_device_operation.cpp:15-74`, `writer_gated_delta_attn.cpp:41-69`, `compute/gated_delta_attn.cpp:105-204`) | `validate_on_program_cache_miss` never validates `BH = shape[0] >= 1` or `NC = shape[1] >= 1`. When `NC == 0`, `reader` pushes 16 `state_tiles` to `dfb_S0` and exits, `compute` pops `dfb_S0` and exits without pushing to `dfb_final_state`, and `writer_gated_delta_attn.cpp:58` (`dfb_final_state_o.wait_front(state_tiles)`) blocks forever | **Permanent device hang on `NC == 0`** and invalid empty `CoreRangeSet` on `BH == 0` |
| **7** | `gated_delta_attn` (`gated_delta_attn_program_factory.cpp:318-323`, `gated_delta_attn_device_operation.cpp:15-74`) | (a) `GatedDeltaAttnSeqProgramFactory::create_program_artifacts` completely ignores `attrs.compute_kernel_config` (which is exposed in the public API and hashed in `operation_attributes_t`) and hardcodes `MathFidelity::HiFi2` and `fp32_dest_acc_en = true`; (b) `validate_tensor` checks `BufferType::DRAM` and `Layout::TILE` but omits `!t.is_sharded()`, cross-device check `t.device() == in.L_unit.device()`, and `attrs.output_mem_config` validation | **User-supplied `compute_kernel_config` (`HiFi4`/`LoFi`/`fp32_dest_acc_en`) is silently dropped** and sharded/cross-device tensors bypass validation |
| **8** | `fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule` (`compute/fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule.cpp:180-226`) | In `for (uint32_t t = 0; t < T; ++t)`, each step pushes `kv` (`16`) updated state tiles into `nxt_S` (`cb_s2` or `cb_s3`) and leaves them unpopped for iteration `t + 1` to pop as `cur_S`. On the final token (`t == T - 1`), `nxt_S` is waited on and read by `mm(cb_q, nxt_S_id, cb_out, ...)` at lines 214–215 but is **never popped** before `kernel_main()` exits | **16 tiles stranded in `cb_s2`/`cb_s3` at kernel exit** and **100% deterministic `~DataflowBuffer() -> finish_impl()` drain deadlock on Quasar** |

---

## Detailed Root-Cause Analysis

### 1. IEEE-754 `-0.0` Bit-Pattern Misclassification in `moe_routing_remap` (`reader_moe_routing_remap.cpp:23, 46, 50-62`)

In `ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/data_movement/moe_routing_remap/device/kernels/dataflow/reader_moe_routing_remap.cpp:23, 46, 50-62`, the reader kernel inspects floating-point routing weights (`BFLOAT16` or `FLOAT32`) by reinterpreting L1 memory as unsigned integers (`ByteSizeAddressType<weight_datum_size_bytes>::type`, i.e., `uint16_t` for 2-byte `bfloat16` or `uint32_t` for 4-byte `float32`):

```cpp
using data_addr_type = ByteSizeAddressType<weight_datum_size_bytes>::type;
...
auto* routing_weights_ptr = reinterpret_cast<volatile tt_l1_ptr data_addr_type*>(routing_weights_l1_base_addr);
uint32_t weight_offset_count = 0;
uint32_t device_weights_count = 0;
for (uint32_t i = 0; i < total_Experts; ++i) {
    data_addr_type val = routing_weights_ptr[i];
    if (val != 0) {
        if (weight_offset_count >= start_non_zero_weight_idx &&
            device_weights_count < num_non_zero_per_device) {
            device_weights_count++;
            *(local_weight_idx_ptr++) = i;
        }
        weight_offset_count++;
    }
}
```

In IEEE-754 floating point, negative zero (`-0.0`) has sign bit `1` and all exponent/mantissa bits `0`:
- `bfloat16(-0.0)` = `0x8000` (`val != 0` is `true`)
- `float32(-0.0)` = `0x80000000` (`val != 0` is `true`)

Whenever an upstream gating, masking, or multiplication op produces `-0.0` for an unselected expert, `val != 0` evaluates to `true`. `reader_moe_routing_remap` records the `-0.0` expert index as an active non-zero expert, increments `weight_offset_count` and `device_weights_count`, and once `device_weights_count == num_non_zero_per_device`, **drops subsequent genuine non-zero experts** in the row (and shifts the partition boundary `weight_offset_count` for all downstream devices in the cluster).

---

### 2. Uninitialized L1 Index OOB `tt_memmove` & Unpopped `DataflowBuffer` Drain Deadlock in `moe_routing_remap` (`writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp:36-64`)

In `ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/data_movement/moe_routing_remap/device/kernels/dataflow/writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp:36-64`:

```cpp
local_weights_dfb.reserve_back(1);
uint32_t local_weights_l1_addr = local_weights_dfb.get_write_ptr();
...
local_weights_dfb.push_back(1);

routing_weights_dfb.wait_front(1);
uint32_t routing_weights_l1_addr = routing_weights_dfb.get_read_ptr();

local_weights_idxs_dfb.wait_front(1);
uint32_t local_weights_idxs_l1_addr = local_weights_idxs_dfb.get_read_ptr();
auto* local_weights_idxs_ptr = reinterpret_cast<volatile tt_l1_ptr idx_addr_type*>(local_weights_idxs_l1_addr);

for (uint32_t i = 0; i < num_non_zero_per_device; ++i) {
    tt_memmove<false, true, false, weight_datum_size_bytes>(
        local_weights_l1_addr + local_weights_idxs_ptr[i] * weight_datum_size_bytes,
        routing_weights_l1_addr + local_weights_idxs_ptr[i] * weight_datum_size_bytes,
        weight_datum_size_bytes);
}
```

Two bugs occur here:
1. **Out-of-bounds L1 corruption**: If the input routing weights contain fewer than `non_zero_weight_size` non-zero values (e.g., when tokens are dropped or router weights are zeroed), `reader_moe_routing_remap.cpp` writes only `device_weights_count < num_non_zero_per_device` entries into `local_weight_idx_ptr`. The remaining slots `local_weights_idxs_ptr[device_weights_count .. num_non_zero_per_device - 1]` contain uninitialized L1 garbage (`uint16_t` up to `65535`). The writer then executes `tt_memmove` to `local_weights_l1_addr + local_weights_idxs_ptr[i] * weight_datum_size_bytes`, corrupting arbitrary L1 memory up to **128 KB (`bfloat16`) or 256 KB (`float32`) past `local_weights_dfb`**.
2. **Unpopped `DataflowBuffer` drain deadlock on Quasar**: `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp` never calls `pop_front(1)` on `routing_weights_dfb`, `local_weights_idxs_dfb`, or `local_weights_dfb`. On Quasar, `DataflowBuffer::~DataflowBuffer()` invokes `finish_impl()`, which blocks waiting for the consumer to pop all pushed entries — causing a **100% deterministic kernel exit deadlock**.

---

### 3. Unaligned L1 CB Allocation (`c_4`, `c_5`) & Unaligned NOC `async_write` in `moe_expert_token_remap` (`moe_expert_token_remap_program_factory.cpp:49-50, 121-145`)

In `ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/data_movement/moe_expert_token_remap/device/moe_expert_token_remap_program_factory.cpp:49-50, 121-145`:
- `c_0..c_3` explicitly align their page sizes to `l1_alignment` (`16` bytes) via `tt::align(..., l1_alignment)`.
- However, `c_4` (`output_mapping_cb_id`) and `c_5` (`output_reduced_cb_id`) set `.total_size` and `.page_size` to raw unaligned `output_mapping_page_size_bytes = experts_per_device * mapping_datum_size_bytes` and `output_reduced_page_size_bytes = experts_per_device * 2`.
- Whenever `experts_per_device * 2` is not a multiple of `16` bytes (for example, `16` total experts across `4` devices -> `experts_per_device = 4` -> `8` bytes per page, or `8` experts across `2` devices), `c_5` is allocated immediately after `c_4` at a **non-16-byte-aligned L1 address** (`addr % 16 == 8`), and `writer_moe_expert_token_remap.cpp:110`:
  ```cpp
  noc.async_write(
      CoreLocalMem<uint32_t>(reduced_l1_addr),
      output_reduced_tensor_Dram,
      output_reduced_page_size_bytes,
      {},
      {.page_id = r});
  ```
  issues a NOC `async_write` from an 8-byte-aligned L1 source address `reduced_l1_addr`, violating the 16-byte NOC L1 alignment requirement.
- Additionally, `MoEExpertTokenRemapDeviceOperation::validate_on_program_cache_miss` (`moe_expert_token_remap_device_operation.cpp:15-78`) never validates:
  - `experts % num_devices == 0` (silently truncating `num_local_experts = experts / num_devices` in `compute_output_specs`),
  - `metadata_shape[2] == topk_shape[2]`, or
  - the shape, dtype, layout, and buffer type of `optional_output_mapping_tensor` and `optional_output_reduced_tensor`.

---

### 4. Unconfigured Extra DRAM Worker Cores Hang Device in `topk_router_gpt` (`topk_router_gpt_program_factory.cpp:91-106, 535, 563`)

In `ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/experimental/topk_router_gpt/device/topk_router_gpt_program_factory.cpp:91-106`:

```cpp
std::vector<CoreCoord> dram_bank2core_coords =
    device->get_optimal_dram_bank_to_logical_worker_assignment(tt::tt_metal::NOC::RISCV_0_default);
const uint32_t num_cores = static_cast<uint32_t>(dram_bank2core_coords.size());
const uint32_t required_cores = (num_cores == 8) ? 8 : 12;
const CoreRangeSet all_cores(dram_bank2core_coords);
```

At line 535, `create_descriptor` creates `{DM0, DM1, COMPUTE}` on **`all_cores`** (`num_cores` cores), but at line 563 it only sets runtime arguments for `required_cores` (`8` or `12`) cores:

```cpp
for (uint32_t ring_pos = 0; ring_pos < required_cores; ring_pos++) { ... }
```

On any device/harvesting configuration where `num_cores > required_cores` (e.g., 9–11 DRAM banks or custom core grids), the remaining `num_cores - required_cores` cores execute `dm0.cpp`, `dm1.cpp`, and `compute.cpp` with default zero runtime arguments (`is_sender = 0, is_worker = 0, is_collector = 0`). In both `compute.cpp:111-127` and `dm1.cpp:115-196`, those unconfigured cores take the `!is_sender` branch and block forever on `dfb_partial_recv.wait_front(num_senders)` and `partial_sem.wait(num_senders)`, **hanging the device**.

---

### 5. Wrong CB ID in `reduce_uninit`, Missing `pack_init` on Quasar, Unbalanced `dfb_index` Pop, and `hidden_dim == 0` in `topk_router_gpt`

1. **Wrong CB passed to `reduce_uninit` (`compute.cpp:252, 287`)**:
   `reduce_uninit(std::uint32_t icb)` in `tt_metal/hw/inc/api/compute/reduce.h:102` takes the **input** CB (`icb`) to restore unpacker configuration. `topk_router_gpt/device/kernels/compute.cpp:252` and `:287` pass the **output** DFB `dfb::reduce_scalar` instead of `dfb::softmax_tmp`.
2. **Missing `#ifdef ARCH_QUASAR pack_init(...); #endif` when switching pack targets (`compute.cpp:118-314`)**:
   `compute.cpp` packs into 7 distinct DFBs (`dfb::local_out`, `dfb::topk_val`, `dfb::intermed_val`, `dfb::intermed_ind`, `dfb::softmax_tmp`, `dfb::reduce_scalar`, `dfb::final_out`) without re-targeting the packer via `pack_init`, causing all packed tiles after startup to route to the initial DFB on Quasar (`#58488`).
3. **Missing `dfb_index.wait_front(1)` and unreserved `get_write_ptr()` in `dm1.cpp`**:
   `dm1.cpp:207, 236, 247, 268` calls `dfb_index.get_read_ptr()` and `dfb_index.pop_front(1)` without ever calling `dfb_index.wait_front(1)` after `dfb_index.push_back(1)` at line 155, leaving the DFB read pointer / consumer state unbalanced. Additionally, `dm1.cpp:113, 210, 219` calls `get_write_ptr()` on `dfb_partial_recv`, `dfb_gathered_val`, and `dfb_gathered_ind` without `reserve_back`.
4. **`hidden_dim == 0` passes validation (`topk_router_gpt_device_operation.cpp:26`)**:
   `TT_FATAL(hidden_dim % 32 == 0, ...)` evaluates `0 % 32 == 0` as `true` without checking `hidden_dim > 0`.

---

### 6. Permanent Device Hang on `NC == 0` (`num_chunks == 0`) & Empty `CoreRangeSet` on `BH == 0` in `gated_delta_attn`

In `ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/transformer/gated_delta_attn/device/gated_delta_attn_device_operation.cpp:36-74`:
- `validate_on_program_cache_miss` validates `shape[2] == CS` and `shape[3] == D` (`128`), but never validates `BH = shape[0] >= 1` or `NC = shape[1] >= 1`.
- When `NC == 0`:
  1. `reader_gated_delta_attn.cpp:146-157` reads the initial state (`16` tiles), calls `dfb_S0_o.push_back(state_tiles)`, skips the `for (uint32_t c = 0; c < NC; ++c)` loop, and exits.
  2. `compute/gated_delta_attn.cpp:106-204` calls `dfb_S0_i.wait_front(state_tiles)`, skips the `c < NC` loop (inside which `dfb_final_state_o.push_back(state_tiles)` is gated on `if (c == NC - 1)` at line 183), pops `dfb_S0_i`, and exits **without pushing anything to `dfb_final_state`**.
  3. `writer_gated_delta_attn.cpp:58` unconditionally executes `dfb_final_state_o.wait_front(state_tiles)` after the `c < NC` loop and **hangs the device forever**.

---

### 7. Ignored `compute_kernel_config` & Missing Sharding/Device Checks in `gated_delta_attn` (`gated_delta_attn_program_factory.cpp:318-323`)

1. `gated_delta_attn_seq` accepts `std::optional<DeviceComputeKernelConfig> compute_kernel_config` and stores it in `operation_attributes_t` (where it affects the program cache key), but `GatedDeltaAttnSeqProgramFactory::create_program_artifacts` (`gated_delta_attn_program_factory.cpp:318-323`) completely ignores `attrs.compute_kernel_config` and hardcodes:
   ```cpp
   ComputeConfig{
       .math_fidelity = tt::tt_metal::MathFidelity::HiFi2,
       .fp32_dest_acc_en = true,
       .math_approx_mode = false,
       .compile_args = compute_ct_args,
   }
   ```
2. `validate_tensor` in `gated_delta_attn_device_operation.cpp:15-26` checks `BufferType::DRAM` and `Layout::TILE` but never checks `!t.is_sharded()`, `t.device() == in.L_unit.device()`, or that `attrs.output_mem_config` is `INTERLEAVED` `DRAM`.

---

### 8. Unpopped `nxt_S` (`cb_s2` / `cb_s3`) on Final Token Step `t == T - 1` in `fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule` (`compute/fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule.cpp:180-226`)

In `ttnn/cpp/ttnn/operations/transformer/fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule/device/kernels/compute/fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule.cpp:180-226`:

```cpp
for (uint32_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
    ...
    uint32_t cur_S_id = (t == 0) ? cb_s : ((t & 1) ? cb_s2 : cb_s3);
    uint32_t nxt_S_id = (t & 1) ? cb_s3 : cb_s2;
    auto& cur_S = (t == 0) ? dfb_s : ((t & 1) ? dfb_s2 : dfb_s3);
    auto& nxt_S = (t & 1) ? dfb_s3 : dfb_s2;
    ...
    cur_S.pop_front(kv);

    // 5. S_new = S_dec + d_upd -> nxt_S
    add_tiles_bcast_SC(cb_s_dec, cb_d_upd, nxt_S_id, k_tiles, v_tiles);
    // add_tiles_bcast_SC reserves and pushes kv (16) tiles into nxt_S

    // 6. o_t = q_t @ S_new -> cb_out
    nxt_S.wait_front(kv);
    mm(cb_q, nxt_S_id, cb_out, 1, k_tiles, v_tiles);
    dfb_q.pop_front(k_tiles);
}
```

In each token step `t`, `add_tiles_bcast_SC` reserves and pushes `kv` (`16`) tiles into `nxt_S`, and step 6 calls `nxt_S.wait_front(kv)` without popping it so that step `t + 1` can consume `nxt_S` as `cur_S` and pop it at line 209. However, on the **final token step (`t == T - 1`)**, no `t + 1` iteration runs, and `kernel_main()` exits without ever calling `nxt_S.pop_front(kv)`. On Quasar, `~DataflowBuffer() -> finish_impl()` on `dfb_s2` / `dfb_s3` blocks forever waiting for those `16` tiles to be popped.

---

## Reproduction

```python
import pytest
import torch
import ttnn


def test_moe_routing_remap_negative_zero_and_partial_nonzero(device):
    # 1. IEEE-754 -0.0bf16 (0x8000) in unselected expert slot
    # Row has 16 experts, 2 active experts (indices 3 and 11), and -0.0 at index 0.
    weights = torch.zeros((1, 1, 1, 16), dtype=torch.bfloat16)
    weights[0, 0, 0, 0] = -0.0  # 0x8000 in bfloat16 — previously misclassified as non-zero!
    weights[0, 0, 0, 3] = 0.625
    weights[0, 0, 0, 11] = 0.375

    tt_weights = ttnn.from_torch(weights, device=device, dtype=ttnn.bfloat16, layout=ttnn.ROW_MAJOR_LAYOUT)
    tt_out = ttnn.moe_routing_remap(tt_weights, non_zero_weight_size=2, expert_parallel_size=1, cluster_axis=0)
    out = ttnn.to_torch(tt_out)

    # Expected: both active experts (3 and 11) preserved; index 0 is 0.0
    assert out[0, 0, 0, 3].item() == pytest.approx(0.625, rel=1e-2)
    assert out[0, 0, 0, 11].item() == pytest.approx(0.375, rel=1e-2)
```

---

## Proposed C++ & Kernel Remediation Patch

The complete, self-contained fix across all 12 affected C++ host and RISC-V/Tensix kernel files is prepared and pushed to fork commit [U-ITACHII/tt-metal@319ff35](https://github.com/U-ITACHII/tt-metal/commit/319ff35a7b5cfc2d5460d6c010ae94c36179d57e) (branch [U-ITACHII:fix/moe-routing-remap-and-gated-delta-defects](https://github.com/U-ITACHII/tt-metal/tree/fix/moe-routing-remap-and-gated-delta-defects)):

1. **`moe_routing_remap` (`reader_moe_routing_remap.cpp`, `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp`)**:
   - Mask out the IEEE-754 sign bit (`val & 0x7FFFu` for 2-byte `bfloat16`, `val & 0x7FFFFFFFu` for 4-byte `float32`) when testing for non-zero routing weights.
   - Initialize unfilled slots in `local_weight_idx_ptr[device_weights_count .. num_non_zero_per_device - 1]` to a sentinel `0xFFFF` and guard `if (idx < total_Experts)` in `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp` before `tt_memmove`.
   - Call `pop_front(1)` on `routing_weights_dfb`, `local_weights_idxs_dfb`, and `local_weights_dfb` before exiting `writer_moe_routing_remap.cpp`.
